WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.531
Lab 1 runs on a Linux control node
with no subscription, and after setup

2
00:00:04.531 --> 00:00:09.013
every outbound request goes to a dead
local proxy, so nothing can leave.

3
00:00:09.013 --> 00:00:11.883
Use a disposable node,
because one step runs

4
00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:15.074
Microsoft's role as root
against the node itself.

5
00:00:15.074 --> 00:00:18.907
First, look at what the database
export becomes: four candidates,

6
00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:22.812
and the Amazon-hosted server tagged
with Ansible for both owners.

7
00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:26.575
Then run Microsoft's role,
unchanged, in check mode.

8
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:31.406
It fails, and the verbose output shows
why: check mode skipped the version check,

9
00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.800
so the role concluded the
agent was already installed.
